# Line-ending policy
#
# The repository stores text files with LF line endings. Working-tree line
# endings follow the developer's platform (CRLF on Windows), so STM32CubeMX
# regenerations on Windows do not show up as whole-file diffs.
# See docs/toolchain.md, section "Line endings".

* text=auto

# Source and build files: always treat as text (some CubeMX-generated files
# contain stray CR characters that would otherwise make Git treat them as
# binary).
*.c       text
*.h       text
*.cpp     text
*.hpp     text
*.s       text
*.S       text
*.ld      text
*.cmake   text
CMakeLists.txt text
*.json    text
*.md      text
*.yml     text
*.yaml    text
*.ioc     text
*.mxproject text

# Files that must keep a specific line ending
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Binary files
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.elf     binary
*.bin     binary
*.hex     binary
